    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      213.55,
      397.31,
      238.89
    ],
    "text": "3.The general objects for which the Corporation isconstituted are hereby declared to be\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Bold",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      172.87,
      249.55,
      397.15,
      286.89
    ],
    "text": "(a)to maintain buildings owned by the Viharaya andto construct and maintain new buildings as andwhen necessary;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      172.87,
      297.55,
      397.68,
      322.89
    ],
    "text": "(b)to conduct activities for the promotion of religiousfavour among Buddhists and the people of the area;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      173.71,
      333.55,
      397.37,
      370.89
    ],
    "text": "(c)to promte, encourage and assist in, activities for thespiritual, cultural, social and physical welfare of itsmembers;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      172.87,
      381.55,
      353.61,
      394.89
    ],
    "text": "(d)to safeguard and propagate Buddhism ;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      173.71,
      405.55,
      397.17,
      442.89
    ],
    "text": "(e)to establish monasteries and forest hermitages andto provide environmental facilities appropriate forthe accomplishment of its objects ;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      175.15,
      453.55,
      397.36,
      490.89
    ],
    "text": "(f)to ordain youth with the requisite qualificationsand religious devotion and to provide them withthe four requisites;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      172.87,
      501.55,
      397.16,
      526.89
    ],
    "text": "(g)to preserve and disseminate the TheravadhiBuddhist philosophy and way of life;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      172.87,
      537.55,
      397.24,
      562.89
    ],
    "text": "(h)to maintain friendly relations with other BuddhistOrganisations, in and outside Sri Lanka;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      175.15,
      573.55,
      397.29,
      610.89
    ],
    "text": "(i)to open a hospital for sick monks and to providemedical facilities to all the monks leading amonastic life;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      175.15,
      621.55,
      397.28,
      670.89
    ],
    "text": "(j)to teach the dhamma and the Vinaya to monks, totrain them in yoga exercises and to make themproficient in Pali, Sinhala and oriental and westernlanguages;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
